            <ArticleTitle>Bifurcation lesion treated with a single stent: a new technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>213-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treatment of bifurcation lesions by percutaneous coronary interventions is one of the challenging issues for the interventional cardiologists. The overall complication rate is higher than nonbifurcation lesions. We describe a new stenting technique for the so-called true bifurcation lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
